@startuml
title DRAFT - UC01 business sequence (no DB locking algorithm)
actor "CSKH System" as C
participant TelecomManagement as T
participant "Customer/Profile" as P
participant "Number Inventory" as N
participant "Activation Outcome" as O
participant "Internal Trigger / Recovery" as R
C -> T : activate(requestId, content, numberMode, waitConsent)
T -> T : validate external JWT, rights, input
alt invalid input or permission
  T --> C : reject; no business side effect
else valid
  T -> O : inspect caller + UC01 + requestId / canonical content
  alt existing requestId, different content
    T --> C : IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT
  else existing requestId, same content
    O --> T : current status / recorded result
    T --> C : replay result, no duplicate side effect
  else new request
    T -> P : resolve external evidence + verified document; compare all supplied profile fields
    alt profile conflict / unverified association
      T --> C : reject; no automatic merge
    else valid profile
      T -> N : request selected / random available number
      alt selected number unavailable / lost race
        T -> O : record FAILED without allocated subscriber
        T --> C : FAILED; no replacement, no WAITING
      else automatic empty pool
        alt no explicit consent
          T -> O : record FAILED
          T --> C : NO_AVAILABLE_NUMBER
        else consent
          T -> O : record WAITING; deadline <= waitingSince + 24h
          T --> C : WAITING + requestId
        end
      else available allocation succeeds
        T -> O : complete number + Subscriber + main Account(0)
        note right of O
          Business invariant: consistent committed outcome;
          no success published before completion.
          Atomic implementation deferred to Phase 4.
        end note
        T --> C : SUCCEEDED + requestId + result
      end
    end
  end
end
== Conditional WAITING processing ==
R -> T : numbers replenished / every60s recovery
T -> O : find eligible WAITING in FIFO order; prioritize over new automatic allocation
alt deadline reached
  T -> O : EXPIRED; must not allocate
else still eligible with consent
  T -> P : recheck eligibility
  T -> N : attempt unique available allocation
  alt eligible and allocation succeeds before expiry
    T -> O : complete once; SUCCEEDED
  else no available number
    T -> O : remain WAITING within deadline
  else business eligibility fails
    T -> O : final FAILED without partial activation
  end
end
== Observation after WAITING / transport timeout ==
note over C,T
  Timeout does not prove rollback.
  A request still processing is not implicitly WAITING.
  Public in-progress response remains Open (OQ-15).
end note
C -> T : query(requestId) / retry same requestId + content
T -> O : read authoritative status
T --> C : authorized result; full replay within7 days after final\nthen tombstone policy (HTTP details Open)
note over T,N
  Concurrent requests for one selected number: at most one succeeds.
  Replenishment/recovery/retry overlap: at most one effect per request.
  FIFO business priority selected; tie-break is detailed design.\n  DB lock algorithm is not shown in this business sequence.\n  RabbitMQ wake-up can duplicate; DB recovery remains authoritative.
end note
@enduml
